              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for to identify, then the Bengali for to uncover."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: সনদ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "সনদ — sônôd — \"a certificate; a charter\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "চাকরির জন্য তোমার সনদ দরকার। chākrir jônyô tomār sônôd dôrkār. You need your certificate for the job."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "সনদ (sônôd) is usually traced to Arabic sanad, something to lean on and so a warrant, through Persian. In Bengali it is a paper that vouches for you: a certificate of a degree, a skill or a grant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
